Merge clean (exit 0, already up to date). Recon done, two files written at worktree root: `PLAN.md` (receipts, every claim cites path:line) and `PLAN.visual.human.unga.md` (plain words for the owner).

Highlights of the recon:
- **Prior dot history**: dots kept as "nested pattern sugar" (LANG.md:37, surface-audit:738), never built. Two prior views never reconciled: dot-as-JOIN (runtime-decomposition:55-84) vs dot-as-projection (extraction-spellings:511-512, the `span.line` ambiguity left open). Q8/left-of-arrow residual still open.
- **No `.` in identifiers** (parse_dl.pl:408-418); `.` is the statement terminator everywhere and lives inside floats. The canonical parser is the DCG; langium demoted to a spelling reference (ARCH.pl:179/249/663, SYNTAX.md:9-11), so a surface change is low cost.
- **Name resolution**: rel names are one flat functor namespace (magic-rel-audit:68); columns bind positional/named by source order (parse_dl.pl:1070-1100); type pass is 0_type_plane.pl struct-as-rows.
- **Lowering**: SQL quotes every identifier (`"spine.files"` is one quoted name, lower.pl:156/195), so dots don't collide with db.table; TS/rx all boxable flat, COUNT-test law holds.
- **(4) namespaces**: today's namespacing already lives off-surface in the SCIP pkg field (typeir PLAN2.md:99); `::` is an ergonomic add with no semantic need.
- **(5) interfaces/traits**: NO. Contracts are already positional column lists (registry.pl:334-399); TS `I` interfaces are host-side only; the one-rel-one-rule-kind law is already dead (ARCH.pl:67). The smallest honest thing (named column list) already exists as type_decl.

The design packet costs four options (one `.`, `::`+`.`, no dots, `::` only). Only the one-symbol inferred design reproduces the TypeSpec model-vs-namespace trap; the plan ends with 5 one-sentence blocking questions and ARCH-style task/3 rows (all unbuilt).

Style check: no em dashes, none of the four banned words (validated by grep).
